[22:34:49] ✓   On real INPOP19a residuals, the central synodic carrier survives at 79.8% after an 82-parameter basis fit, while the mean sideband survival is 95.7%. For the synthetic dynamically modulated TEP signal, carrier survival is 80.4% and sideband mean survival is 96.0%. The sidebands (D±M, D±annual) are substantially more robust to absorption than the central carrier because the basis lacks explicit cross-frequency product terms. This spectral persistence is direct evidence that the residual signal carries a dynamical sideband signature that cannot be reproduced by static ephemeris parameter adjustments.
